# Ternary Bonsai 2.5 27B vs Ternary Bonsai 2 27B on the GTX 1070 Ti

Generated by `bench/bonsai25_vs_2.sh` (summary: `bench/bonsai25_vs_2_summary.py`). Engine runs: temp 0, seed 42, `taskset -c 0-3`, one GPU program at a time, VRAM cap 7373 MiB. Peak VRAM = highest `nvidia-smi` sample, RSS = max resident set of the engine process. A dagger marks a Bonsai 2 number taken from an earlier recorded run (other session) instead of this run.

## 1. Files and head tensors

| file | size (B) | block_count | tensors | tokenizer tokens | tokenizer sha256 (first 12) | blk.64/nextn tensors | blk.0 ssm_alpha / ssm_beta |
|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---|
| `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf` | 5,946,648,928 | 64 | 851 | 248320 | 49930cc8a751 | 0 | BF16 / BF16 |
| `Ternary-Bonsai-2.5-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf` | 5,993,834,848 | 64 | 851 | 248320 | 49930cc8a751 | 0 | F32 / F32 |
| `Ternary-Bonsai-2.5-27B-PTQ1_0-mtp.gguf` | 6,232,818,944 | 65 | 866 | 248320 | 49930cc8a751 | 15 | F32 / F32 |

Full tensor names, types and shapes: `probe.txt`. Same tokenizer hash on both models means the shared long prompts are valid for both.

**Type diff, Bonsai 2 versus each Bonsai 2.5 file** (tensors present in both whose ggml type differs):

- `Ternary-Bonsai-2.5-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf`: BF16 -> F32 for 96 tensors (e.g. `blk.0.ssm_alpha.weight`, `blk.0.ssm_beta.weight`)
- `Ternary-Bonsai-2.5-27B-PTQ1_0-mtp.gguf`: BF16 -> F32 for 96 tensors (e.g. `blk.0.ssm_alpha.weight`, `blk.0.ssm_beta.weight`)

## 2. Gates and load check

- SASS gate: `SASS gate: PASS`
- ternary_ab_test: `ternary_ab_test: 180 cases, 180 bit-identical, 0 differ -> PASS`

- Bonsai 2: 48 tokens, 19 distinct ids, decode 17.33 tok/s, text: ` Paris. The capital of Germany is Berlin. The capital of Italy is Rome. The capital of Spain is Madrid. The capital of Portugal is Lisbon. The capital of the Un`
- Bonsai 2.5: 2 tokens, 2 distinct ids, decode 15.73 tok/s, text: ` Paris.`

